    icon: '💡',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Don't 'dump' your easiest cards early. If you see a way to play a 7 of Hearts, wait until you have another card that depends on it. The more cards you put on the table, the more options your OPPONENTS have on their turns.\n\nThe Big Reveal: Wait until you can play 4-5 cards at once by rearranging the whole board. This 'explodes' your hand and often ends the game before opponents can react to the new board state.\n\nDefensive Manipulation: If you see an opponent looking for a 5 of Spades to finish their sequence, and that 5 is already in a 'Set of 5s' on the table, try to move that 5 into a DIFFERENT sequence that is harder for them to access.",
    Player: "Don't 'dump' your easiest cards early. If you see a way to play a 7 of Hearts, wait until you have another card that depends on it. The more cards you put on the table, the more options your OPPONENTS have on their turns.\n\nThe Big Reveal: Wait until you can play 4-5 cards at once by rearranging the whole board. This 'explodes' your hand and often ends the game before opponents can react to the new board state.\n\nDefensive Manipulation: If you see an opponent looking for a 5 of Spades to finish their sequence, and that 5 is already in a 'Set of 5s' on the table, try to move that 5 into a DIFFERENT sequence that is harder for them to access.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
    riskTolerance: 0.5,
    bluffFrequency: 0.3,
    bluffSettings: {
      profile: 'balanced',
    },
    basic: "Don't 'dump' your easiest cards early. If you see a way to play a 7 of Hearts, wait until you have another card that depends on it. The more cards you put on the table, the more options your OPPONENTS have on their turns.",
    intermediate: "The Big Reveal: Wait until you can play 4-5 cards at once by rearranging the whole board. This 'explodes' your hand and often ends the game before opponents can react to the new board state.",
    advanced: "Defensive Manipulation: If you see an opponent looking for a 5 of Spades to finish their sequence, and that 5 is already in a 'Set of 5s' on the table, try to move that 5 into a DIFFERENT sequence that is harder for them to access.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Sequences are better for manipulation than Sets. A sequence of 3-4-5-6 can be split into two 3-card melds if you have the right cards; a 3-card Set is 'atomic' and cannot be split.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Always scan for 'orphan' cards. If you see a sequence of 4 cards, you can potentially take one end and use it elsewhere.",
      },
    ],
